From: Transom contributors
Subject: [PATCH] urbdrc: don't crash when a USB device can't be opened

udev_init() frees a half-initialised device on failure (for example when
libusb_open() returns LIBUSB_ERROR_ACCESS), before request_queue exists.
udev_free() then calls ArrayList_Count(NULL) and the client crashes.

---
--- a/channels/urbdrc/client/libusb/libusb_udevice.c
+++ b/channels/urbdrc/client/libusb/libusb_udevice.c
@@ -1787,7 +1787,7 @@
 		log_libusb_result(urbdrc->log, WLOG_ERROR, "libusb_reset_device", rc);
 	}
 
-	while (ArrayList_Count(udev->request_queue) > 0)
+	while (udev->request_queue && (ArrayList_Count(udev->request_queue) > 0))
 	{
 		/* HACK: We need to wait until the cancel transfer has been processed by
 		 * poll_libusb_events
